@startuml
title UC9 - PvP Battle - Test Cases

map "TC-UC9-01: Win PvP battle" as TC1 {
  Test Case Number => TC-UC9-01
  Test Case Name => Successfully win a PvP battle
  Description => Verify player can win PvP battle and stats are updated correctly
  Preconditions => 1. Both players matched via UC8 \n 2. BattleRoom created \n 3. Both connected via SignalR
  Test Case Input => Player 1: Charizard (Lv.50) \n Player 2: Blastoise (Lv.45) \n Action: Attack (Flamethrower)
  Expected Output => 1. Battle proceeds with turn-based mechanics \n 2. Opponent Pokemon defeated \n 3. Player 1 wins \n 4. PvPWins incremented \n 5. Results saved to MySQL
  Steps => 1. BattleRoom initializes with both teams \n 2. Both players select actions \n 3. Server determines turn order by Speed \n 4. Attacks executed sequentially \n 5. Opponent Pokemon faints \n 6. Verify winner declared \n 7. Verify PvPWins updated \n 8. Verify results saved to MySQL
  Default Value Preserving => Winner PvPWins +1, Loser PvPLosses +1 in MySQL
}

map "TC-UC9-02: Opponent disconnects during battle" as TC2 {
  Test Case Number => TC-UC9-02
  Test Case Name => Win by default when opponent disconnects
  Description => Verify player wins by default when opponent connection is lost
  Preconditions => 1. PvP battle is in progress \n 2. Both players connected
  Test Case Input => Opponent connection: disconnected at turn 3
  Expected Output => 1. System detects opponent disconnect \n 2. Player wins by default \n 3. PvPWins incremented \n 4. Return to Main Menu
  Steps => 1. Battle in progress at turn 3 \n 2. Opponent connection drops \n 3. Server detects disconnect timeout \n 4. Verify player declared winner by default \n 5. Verify PvPWins updated \n 6. Verify return to Main Menu
  Default Value Preserving => Winner PvPWins +1, disconnected player PvPLosses +1
}

@enduml
